---
/**
 * "Run it yourself" and "Automate it": the open-source CLI path, placed right
 * under the hero on purpose. The workflow mirrors
 * .github/workflows/afdocs-scheduled.yml, which runs against promptless.ai.
 */
import { Copy } from '@lucide/astro';
import { AFDOCS_REPO_URL, AFDOCS_SITE_URL, AUTHOR_URL, SPEC_URL } from '@lib/agent-score/meta';

const command = 'npx afdocs@latest check https://docs.example.com --format scorecard';

const workflow = `name: Agent Score
on:
  schedule:
    - cron: '0 17 * * *' # daily
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  afdocs:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 10
    steps:
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 22
      - name: Score docs with afdocs
        run: |
          set +e
          OUTPUT=$(npx -y afdocs@latest check "https://docs.example.com" \\
            --format json --score --sampling deterministic)
          set -e
          SCORE=$(printf '%s' "$OUTPUT" | jq -r '.scoring.overall // empty')
          if [ -z "$SCORE" ]; then
            echo "::error::Could not parse the afdocs score"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "Agent Score: $SCORE"
          if [ "$SCORE" -lt 90 ]; then
            echo "::error::Agent Score $SCORE is below 90"
            exit 1
          fi`;

const vitest = `// agent-docs.test.ts
// Reads the url from agent-docs.config.yml
import { describeAgentDocsPerCheck } from 'afdocs/helpers';

describeAgentDocsPerCheck();`;
---

<section class="pl-as-section pl-as-section-tight" id="run-it-yourself" aria-labelledby="pl-as-diy-title">
  <div class="pl-as-diy">
    <div>
      <p class="pl-as-eyebrow">Open source</p>
      <h2 class="pl-as-h2" id="pl-as-diy-title">Run it yourself</h2>
      <p class="pl-as-lede">
        Agent Score is a hosted run of afdocs. Run the same command from your terminal and you get the same checks and
        the same scoring, with a fix for every issue when you add <code>--fixes</code>. Requires Node 22 or later.
      </p>
      <p class="pl-as-credit">
        <a href={AFDOCS_REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track-action="view_afdocs" data-track-funnel="education" data-track-location="agent_score_diy">afdocs</a>{' '}
        is open source (MIT) by{' '}
        <a href={AUTHOR_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track-action="view_afdocs_author" data-track-funnel="education" data-track-location="agent_score_diy">Dachary Carey</a>{' '}
        and implements the{' '}
        <a href={SPEC_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track-action="view_agent_docs_spec" data-track-funnel="education" data-track-location="agent_score_diy">Agent-Friendly Docs Spec</a>.
        Promptless did not write it; we run it.
      </p>
      <ul class="pl-as-links">
        <li><a href={AFDOCS_REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/agent-ecosystem/afdocs</a></li>
        <li><a href={AFDOCS_SITE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">afdocs.dev</a></li>
        <li><a href={SPEC_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">agentdocsspec.com</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="pl-as-terminal pl-as-terminal-lg">
      <div class="pl-as-terminal-bar">
        <span class="pl-as-terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span class="pl-as-terminal-title pl-as-mono-label">terminal</span>
        <button class="pl-as-btn pl-as-btn-ghost" type="button" data-as-copy data-as-copy-text={command} aria-label="Copy the afdocs command">
          <Copy size={14} aria-hidden="true" /><span data-as-copy-label>Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre class="pl-as-scorecard-preview"><code><span class="pl-as-prompt">$ </span><span class="pl-as-strong">{command}</span>

Agent-Friendly Docs Scorecard
==============================

  Overall Score: <span class="pl-as-strong">82 / 100 (B)</span>

  Content Discoverability        74 / 100 (C)
  Markdown Availability          63 / 100 (D)
  Page Size and Truncation Risk  92 / 100 (A)
  <span class="pl-as-comment">…</span>

  <span class="pl-as-warn">WARN</span>  llms-txt-directive-html   No llms.txt directive found…
  <span class="pl-as-ok">PASS</span>  rendering-strategy        All 50 sampled pages contain…</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pl-as-section pl-as-section-tight" id="automate" aria-labelledby="pl-as-automate-title">
  <p class="pl-as-eyebrow">Keep it there</p>
  <h2 class="pl-as-h2" id="pl-as-automate-title">Automate it</h2>
  <p class="pl-as-lede">
    Scores drift when docs change. Run afdocs on a schedule and fail the build when the score drops below your bar.
    This is the workflow we run against promptless.ai every day.
  </p>
  <div class="pl-as-automate">
    <div class="pl-as-terminal">
      <div class="pl-as-terminal-bar">
        <span class="pl-as-terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span class="pl-as-terminal-title pl-as-mono-label">.github/workflows/agent-score.yml</span>
        <button class="pl-as-btn pl-as-btn-ghost" type="button" data-as-copy data-as-copy-target="#pl-as-workflow" aria-label="Copy the GitHub Actions workflow">
          <Copy size={14} aria-hidden="true" /><span data-as-copy-label>Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre><code id="pl-as-workflow">{workflow}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="pl-as-automate-side">
      <div class="pl-as-terminal">
        <div class="pl-as-terminal-bar">
          <span class="pl-as-terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span class="pl-as-terminal-title pl-as-mono-label">vitest</span>
          <button class="pl-as-btn pl-as-btn-ghost" type="button" data-as-copy data-as-copy-target="#pl-as-vitest" aria-label="Copy the vitest helper">
            <Copy size={14} aria-hidden="true" /><span data-as-copy-label>Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre><code id="pl-as-vitest">{vitest}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="pl-as-note pl-as-panel">
        <strong>Same numbers, here and in CI.</strong> The hosted scanner runs the identical command,{' '}
        <code>afdocs check &lt;url&gt; --format json --score</code>, with <code>--sampling deterministic</code> so the same pages are sampled every time. Pin the afdocs version shown on your report to match it exactly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
